%T A398911 1428055454246576,526199853838356628,236887165279834828587,
%U A398911 127947330306503512748168,81653493881924418175152638,60787071477215875281659605104
%N A398911 Number of partitions of {1,...,3*n} into 3-element subsets {x,y,z} such that the sums x+y+z are all distinct.
%H A398911 Meghanto Majumder, <a href="/A398911/a398911.txt">C program used to compute a(10)-a(14) through inclusion-exclusion</a>
%F A398911 a(n) = Sum_{S subset of [3n]} (-1)^|S| * e_n(c_6(S), ..., c_{9n-3}(S)), where c_s(S) is the number of triples {x,y,z} with x+y+z = s and none of x, y, z in S, and e_n denotes the elementary symmetric polynomial of degree n (choose n distinct sums and one surviving triple from each). Configurations that miss an element cancel, leaving a partition of {1,...,3n} into n disjoint triples with distinct sums. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Aug 15 2026
%e A398911 For n=2, all binomial(6,3)/2 = 10 partitions qualify, since 1+...+6 = 21 is odd.
%Y A398911 Cf. A203017, A320129.
%K A398911 nonn,more,changed
%O A398911 0,3
